---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Privacy policy — Milton"
  description="Milton is operated by Zone of Danger, LLC (“we”)."
  legal
>
  <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
  <p class="updated">
    Last updated: <time datetime="2026-10-30">October 30, 2026</time>
  </p>
  <p>Milton is operated by Zone of Danger, LLC (“we”).</p>

  <h2>What Milton stores</h2>
  <p>
    Your name and email address from Google or GitHub when you sign in; the
    recipes you and your assistants write, every version of each, who wrote it
    and when; which assistants you have connected; and a daily count of tool
    calls.
  </p>

  <h2>How we use it</h2>
  <p>
    Only to run Milton — to sign you in, keep your recipes and their history,
    and serve them to the assistants you connect. We do not sell your data, show
    ads, or use your recipes to train AI models.
  </p>

  <h2>Who can see your recipes</h2>
  <p>You, and the assistants you connect.</p>

  <h2>Where it is kept</h2>
  <p>
    The database and sign-in run on Neon (United States); the website and server
    run on Vercel; DNS is on Cloudflare. Google and GitHub handle your sign-in
    with them.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>Only the ones that keep you signed in.</p>

  <h2>Deleting your data</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href="mailto:peter@meetmilton.com">peter@meetmilton.com</a> and we
    will delete your account and its history. Backups age out within the
    database provider's retention period.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>We will update the date above when this policy changes.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    <a href="mailto:peter@meetmilton.com">peter@meetmilton.com</a>.
  </p>
</SiteLayout>
